# NOTICE — Protocol & Clean-Room Attribution

## Reticulum Wire Protocol Attribution
BIFROST — The Reticulum Ghost Browser implements communication over the **Public Domain Reticulum Wire Protocol**, invented and published into the public domain by Danish engineer **Mark Qvist** (<https://reticulum.network>).

We give full technical credit to Mark Qvist for creating the Reticulum cryptographic networking architecture.

## Clean-Room MIT Rust Transport Stack
To maintain full OSI open-source and commercial licensing clarity across enterprise, industrial (EU ESPR / CIRPASS-2), and defense deployments, BIFROST does **not** bundle or depend on Mark Qvist's post-April-2025 Python `RNS` package.

All wire-level Reticulum transport, Curve25519 key exchange (X25519 ECDH + Ed25519 signatures), HDLC framing, and flow control are provided by clean-room, MIT-licensed Rust crates:
- `citadel-rns-rs` (<https://github.com/whattio/citadel-rns-rs>, MIT License)
- `reticulum-rs` (MIT License)
- `ed25519-dalek` & `sha2` (RustCrypto, MIT / Apache-2.0)
- `wry` & `tao` (Tauri Programme within The Commons Conservancy, MIT / Apache-2.0)

